## T0384 — App Email configuration for Administrators

**State at plan:** `ready` · **Depends on:** none

There is no mail transport in the app. Administration is the modal in `client/src/components/shell/AdministrationModal.tsx` (`ADMIN_SECTIONS` in `client/src/lib/administration.tsx`). The durable queue is pg-boss (`src/services/jobs/queue.ts`), shipped in T0206.

### Scope

- New Administration section for outbound mail through an external service: host, port, encryption, account username, password, and API token, plus From address, From name, Reply-to, and a timeout in seconds.
- Sender display name (for example TaskMesh) separate from the envelope From address.
- Secrets stored server-side and not returned in full on later reads.
- A send path later members call. This Task proves it with a configuration save and a connection or test send an administrator can run.
- An email transaction log: time, result, To, Subject, and server warnings and errors. Message body is not stored. Surface it in the existing Administration logging area.
- Administration graphs for email failures and activity (sends, retries, queue depth), using the same job metrics as the pg-boss queue where a send is queued.

### Out of scope

- Signup, notification templates, preferences, reminders, and digest rendering (later members).
- Inbound mail.

### QA follow-ups

- Connection settings: Port and Encryption share one row. Server account authentication: Username and Password share one row. Each pair stacks on viewports 640px and narrower.
- Enable outbound email and the “Mail settings saved” notice sit on the same row as Save and Test connection.

## T0129 — User email self-signup process

**State at plan:** `ready` · **Depends on:** T0111 (complete, outside this epic)

Login is `client/src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`. Administrators already create email-and-password users. Password rules live in `src/lib/password.ts` and `client/src/lib/password.ts` (length, classes, repeats, sequences, history).

### Scope

- When email self-signup is enabled, the login screen offers signup by email.
- The email field checks address format before submit. The password field uses the existing complexity rules.
- The server sends a confirmation message through the T0384 transport. The link activates the account. Until confirmation, the account cannot sign in.
- Disable the path when mail is not configured or self-signup is turned off. Administrators keep the existing create-user path.

### Out of scope

- OAuth and OIDC changes (T0111 is already complete).
- Notification preferences and digest mail.

### QA follow-ups

## T0221 — Notifications: templates, preferences and scheduled delivery

**State at plan:** `blocked` (open Depends-on is T0384, inside this epic) · **Depends on:** T0206 (complete, outside), T0384 (in epic)

Builds on the parent mail capability and the pg-boss queue.

### Scope

- Notification types registered in code: digest, reminder, mention, assignment. Each has an HTML template, a plain-text template, and an in-app form.
- Per-user preferences: which types, channel (in-app, email), frequency, quiet hours, and time zone.
- Sends go through the shared job queue with retries. Every send is written to the T0384 email log.
- Due-date and action-by reminders for Tasks and ToDos.
- One-click unsubscribe per type.

### Out of scope

- Rendering a stored AI digest into that email (T0218).
- Administrator SMTP configuration (T0384).

### QA follow-ups

- Inbox cards now show **Unread** or **Read**. Unread cards keep an accent bar and tint; read cards are dimmer. Marking read updates the card immediately. A notice whose link is the inbox itself stays on this page and only changes read state. A notice that points at a task or to-do still opens that record.

